{
 "id": "page-ordination-science",
 "target": "page",
 "page": "ordination.html",
 "goal": "On the ordination page: the two-gradient demo parses to 20 sites x 24 species, NMDS in 2 dimensions carries a stress with Clarke's bands, the Shepard diagram fits 190 pairs (20*19/2), PCoA reports axis percentages over positive eigenvalues only with negative eigenvalues counted for a semi-metric; the no-structure demo will not help you read the picture; three sites are refused (four minimum); four sites at k=2 fit exactly by construction at stress 0.000 with the free-coordinates warning, five sites without it; an empty site, an unreadable value and a quoted comma in a species name are each named, not swallowed. Then every NMDS setting is driven from its own pane -- the square-root transform chip, the Bray-Curtis dissimilarity, the dimensions and the random-starts steppers -- each returned to its default so the seeded ordination is unchanged, and the quoted-data parse is read once more. Then the page's three exports are read: the copied dissimilarity matrix is the 4x4 Bray-Curtis of the square-rooted, Wisconsin-standardised quoted data to six decimals, byte for byte (X to Y 0.189902, X to W 0.101337, Y to Z 0.480846, zeros on the diagonal); the copied coordinates carry site,NMDS1,NMDS2, one row per site and the page's own warning that NMDS axes are arbitrary with stress-1 = 0.0000, and no NaN; and the print button prints.",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "look",
   "action": "observe",
   "expect": {
    "ok": true,
    "snapshot.page": "ordination.html"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "data",
   "action": "show-pane",
   "arguments": {
    "pane": "p-data"
   },
   "expect": {
    "ok": true
   }
  },
